# extra_bg1_metatiles
# The extra stage's own metatiles (book: Stage 2: Collapsed Tower), after
# stage 1's two streams: the climb's tower facade, interior and broken
# edges, and the slabs, pillars and power line of the climb drawn over
# them (their blank $0260 tiles replaced by the wall's). Only stage 1's
# characters below $391 (no collision class) are added; the collision
# tiles are those of the metatiles they come from.
# 34 metatiles, $1A8-$1C9 (tools/levelmap.py metatiles)
# Side-view metatiles: 4x4 tiles each, as draw_bg_column / draw_bg_row read
# them. One line per metatile: its number (hex), then its 4 rows of 4 BG
# tilemap words, top row first, rows separated by "|". A word is
# vhopppcc cccccccc: $8000 v (vertical flip), $4000 h (horizontal flip),
# $2000 o (priority), $1C00 ppp (palette 0-7), $03FF c (character 0-1023).
# The map names a metatile by its number (map word = number * $20, plus the
# flip bits). Which tiles collide is decided by the tile number (c), per
# stage (book: Side-view collision map).
1A8: 115C 115C 115C 115C | 0DBB 0DBB 0DBB 0DBB | 0DBB 0DBB 0DBB 0DBB | 0DBB 0DBB 0DBB 0DBB
1A9: 115C 115C 115C 115C | 0A80 0A81 0A82 0A82 | 0BF1 0BF1 0BF3 0BF3 | 0A77 0A78 0A79 0A79
